  "status": "No Objection to Proposal (OBS only)",
  "description": "The works relate to two plants which have become overgrown and are beginning to cause issues for neighbouring properties. Neither have a TPO.&nbsp;Rear garden – large overgrown palm (palmetto)&nbsp;- Approximately 6m tall, non-woody trunk.- Now encroaching on the boundary and blocking light to the adjoining property.- Parts of the plant are already dying back.Proposal: remove the palm completely and replant with a smaller shrub more appropriate to the setting.Front garden – common elder shrub (sambucus)- An elder that has grown well beyond normal shrub scale and now forms a small tree.- Located close to the boundary wall and footpath.Proposal: reduce by 50%. Up to 4m from branch tipsThese works are intended to tidy and improve the front and rear gardens and have minimal impact on the public realm.",
